    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d296-a1">

                <pb facs="0826" n="612" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg612"/>

                <head>Mr. Hoyt to Mr. Nelson</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Consulate of the United States of
                                America</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Minatitlan,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1871-01-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 11, 1871.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to inform you that Colonel
                    J. J. Williams, and his corps of engineers, assisted by all the federal and
                    local authorities in this port, broke ground for the <pb facs="0827" n="613"
                        xml:id="pg613"/> New York Tehuantepec Railway, carriage-road, and telegraph
                    line at a point about half a mile from this place, on the 9th of the present
                    month. I had the honor of being present. The ceremony, including the speech of
                    Colonel Williams, was very interesting, and was well attended by natives and
                    foreigners.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. C. M. HOYT, <hi rendition="#italic">United States
                        Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
